body:
In [UrlRule.php:238](https://github.com/yiisoft/yii2/blob/master/framework/web/UrlRule.php#L238) you will get the following call:

``` php
preg_match("#^search-vuz/(?P<page>\d+)/(?P<per-page>[^\/]+)$#u", 'search-vuz/2/3', $matches);
```

PHP does not allow to use `-` in named groups for regexp: https://3v4l.org/NWC2g.
@cebe I don't know, how to fix it easily.

Also it's not working with [alternative named group syntax](http://php.net/manual/en/function.preg-match.php#refsect1-function.preg-match-changelog):

``` php
preg_match("#^search-vuz/(?<page>\d+)/(?<per-page>[^\/]+)$#u", 'search-vuz/2/3', $matches);
preg_match("#^search-vuz/(?'page'\d+)/(?'per-page'>[^\/]+)$#u", 'search-vuz/2/3', $matches);
```

Both of lines caused `Compilation failed: syntax error in subpattern name`

We can replace group name with placeholder and then restore it. It will be something like this:

``` php
$tr3 = ['d495b570' => 'page', 'b2ce9e4a' => 'per-page'];
preg_match("#^search-vuz/(?P<d495b570>\d+)/(?P<b2ce9e4a>[^\/]+)$#u", 'search-vuz/2/3', $matches);
foreach ($matches as $key => $match) {
    if (isset($tr3[$key]) {
        $matches[$tr3[$key]] = $match;
        unset($matches[$key]);
    }
}
```

